torOS: show the boot logo on a quiet boot too.

fbcon leaves the logo out when the kernel is started with "quiet", so that a
firmware picture is not replaced by a penguin. torOS wants exactly that
replacement: its own logo and no messages.

--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c	2026-10-06 07:34:27.340563383 +0300
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c	2026-10-06 07:34:27.347984338 +0300
@@ -1036,9 +1036,6 @@
 
 	info = fbcon_info_from_console(vc->vc_num);
 
-	if (logo_shown < 0 && console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET)
-		logo_shown = FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW;
-
 	if (vc != svc || logo_shown == FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW ||
 	    (info->fix.type == FB_TYPE_TEXT))
 		logo = 0;
